---

# 179. AI Dependency Injection

AI providers devem ser injetados.

Não criar clients diretamente nos services.

---

# 180. AI Configuration via Dependency Injection

Permitir:

```text
mock provider
test provider
production provider
```

sem alterar regra de negócio.

---

# 181. Testing AI Components

Testes devem incluir:

```text
unit
integration
contract
evaluation
security
```

---

# 182. Mock LLM

Testes determinísticos devem utilizar mock/fake LLM quando não for necessário chamar provider real.

---

# 183. AI Integration Tests

Poucos testes devem chamar providers reais.

Devem ser:

```text
controlled
expensive-aware
isolated
```

---

# 184. AI Contract Tests

Validar:

```text
request
response
schema
provider adapter
error normalization
```

---

# 185. AI Security Tests

Testar:

```text
prompt injection
tool abuse
tenant leakage
PII leakage
unauthorized tool
budget bypass
rate limit bypass
```

---

# 186. RAG Security Tests

Testar explicitamente:

```text
tenant isolation
document permissions
metadata filters
cross-user retrieval
deleted documents
```

---

# 187. Agent Security Tests

Testar:

```text
unauthorized tool
tool escalation
prompt injection
loop
budget exhaustion
permission bypass
```

---

# 188. AI Load Testing

Workloads críticos devem avaliar:

```text
concurrency
provider rate limits
queue behavior
latency
cost
failure recovery
```

---

# 189. AI Chaos Testing

Quando necessário, simular:

```text
provider unavailable
slow provider
invalid output
rate limit
network failure
partial failure
```

---

# 190. AI Operational Dashboard

Quando relevante, dashboard deve mostrar:

```text
requests
success rate
latency
tokens
cost
provider
model
fallbacks
errors
guardrail blocks
quality metrics
```

---

# 191. AI Cost Dashboard

Mostrar:

```text
total cost
cost by tenant
cost by user
cost by feature
cost by model
cost by provider
```

---

# 192. AI Quality Dashboard

Mostrar:

```text
evaluation score
feedback
hallucination indicators
retrieval quality
output validation failures
```

---

# 193. AI Model Registry

Registry deve permitir:

```text
model
provider
capabilities
limits
pricing
status
approved
deprecated
```

---

# 194. Approved Model Policy

Somente modelos aprovados devem ser utilizados em produção.

---

# 195. Experimental Models

Modelos experimentais devem ser explicitamente marcados:

```text
experimental: true
```

---

# 196. AI Environment Policy

Development:

```text
mock / cheap models
```

Staging:

```text
controlled provider access
```

Production:

```text
approved models only
```

---

# 197. AI Production Gate

Antes de produção:

```text
[ ] Provider approved
[ ] Model approved
[ ] Prompt version approved
[ ] Evaluation passed
[ ] Security review
[ ] Cost reviewed
[ ] Rate limits
[ ] Guardrails
[ ] Observability
[ ] Audit
[ ] Rollback strategy
```

---

# 198. AI Change Management

Alterações em:

```text
model
provider
prompt
RAG
embedding
retriever
agent
tool
guardrail
```

devem ser tratadas como mudanças de software potencialmente impactantes.

---

# 199. AI Change Record

Registrar:

```text
what changed
why
who
previous version
new version
evaluation result
risk
rollback
```

---

