# 235. Olivelas Backend Security Standard

O backend Olivelas deve ser construído assumindo que:

```text
Clients are untrusted.
Networks are untrusted.
Tokens can be compromised.
Users can be malicious.
Tenants must be isolated.
External APIs can fail.
LLMs are probabilistic and untrusted.
Dependencies can contain vulnerabilities.
```

Portanto:

```text
Identity
+
Authorization
+
Isolation
+
Validation
+
Encryption
+
Audit
+
Observability
+
Testing
+
Incident Response
```

devem formar uma única arquitetura de segurança.

---

# 236. Final Principle

Segurança não deve ser implementada como:

```text
API
+
Authentication
```

A arquitetura deve evoluir para:

```text
API
│
├── Identity
├── Authentication
├── Authorization
├── RBAC
├── ABAC
├── Tenant Isolation
├── Data Security
├── Secrets
├── Rate Limiting
├── Input Validation
├── Audit
├── Observability
├── Threat Modeling
├── Security Testing
├── Supply Chain Security
├── AI Security
└── Incident Response
```

O princípio final é:

```text
Security is not a feature.
Security is an architectural property.
```

E:

```text
Never Trust.
Always Verify.
Least Privilege.
Default Deny.
Fail Secure.
Audit Everything Important.
```

O Olivelas Backend deve ser **secure by design, zero-trust by default, tenant-aware, API-first e AI-ready**, mantendo segurança como uma preocupação transversal a todos os Volumes I–V.', '["backend", "sdd", "spec", "fastapi", "loft-standard"]'::jsonb, '["cmp_be_auth_service", "cmp_be_permission_service"]'::jsonb, '["rul_loft_be_api_envelope", "rul_loft_be_error_codes"]'::jsonb, '["tpl_loft_admin_backoffice"]'::jsonb, '["arch_loft_standard_fullstack"]'::jsonb, '["mod_auth_identity_be"]'::jsonb, '[{"version": "1.0.0", "date": "2026-09-01", "note": "Versão inicial canônica"}]'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, summary = EXCLUDED.summary, content = EXCLUDED.content;
